{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>אף חבב עמים</b> in gematria is גרים (212). For converts who are destined to convert stood at Sinai. And similarly: את אשר ישנו פה. The letters ס' ת' stand for תורה. For all of them were there at the time of the giving of the Torah. And it says in the language of אף, because it speaks of those who suffer afflictions on account of words of Torah:" "<b>קדושיו</b> twice in the Masorah: כל קדושיו בידך · יראו את ה' קדושיו. Why do they fear YHWH's holy ones? For all His holy ones are in your hand:" "<b>תכו</b> twice in the Masorah: והם תכו לרגלך · על מה תכו. There the meaning is striking; here too the meaning is striking. To teach that they are struck to enter and walk after you:" "<b>תכו לרגלך ישא מדברותיך</b> — the initial letters (ר\"ת) spell תלים. For upon every tip of every letter you suspend mounds of halakhot:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:25.325478244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}